From 68e5a4efeaae77204f9ea699fbfa96a6a2340cf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:06:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the guest's pacman layer through omarchy refresh pacman

omarchy refresh pacman, which channel switches and package reinstalls run, copies Omarchy's stable templates over pacman.conf and the mirrorlist, then runs a downgrade-capable -Syyuu. The templates leave out the local try-omarchy repository, the linux and linux-headers hold and the guest's Arch mirrors, so the transaction tried to move the system to Omarchy's stable mirror snapshot and was refused (aquamarine 0.15.1 breaks the runtime's dependency). The disk was left on that snapshot without the local repository or the hold.

A reviewed patch to omarchy-refresh-pacman has the new pacman-layer helper put the hold, the local repository and the Arch mirrors back right after Omarchy writes its templates, before the user hook and the transaction. The Arch mirrorlist is the one Omarchy saved as .bak when it is the guest's own, otherwise the image's copy. Both downgrade-capable transactions (refresh and reinstall) ignore an installed managed rebuild while Arch offers the same or an older version, so -uu keeps the patched aquamarine, and a newer Arch release still replaces it.

Compatibility revision 71 repairs disks a refused refresh already rewrote: when pacman.conf has no try-omarchy repository and the mirrorlist names only Omarchy's mirrors, catch-up restores pacman.conf.bak when it is the guest's own, otherwise adds the layer, and restores the Arch mirrors. Other configurations are left alone and no package transaction runs. Runtime 4.5.0-16 carries the patched commands.
